WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.710
Whether for internal customers or external
customers, etiquette and professional conduct

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.290
are very important when troubleshooting a
network situation.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.240
Think about it: Having any part of a network
down is a high-stress situation.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.660
We, as network administrators, want to calm
the situation down, not make it worse.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.970
Thus, here are some key factors to follow
as they relate to etiquette and professional

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:22.990
conduct.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.340
First, avoid jargon.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.510
Explanations to customers should be clear
and concise.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:33.170
Secondly, maintain a positive attitude and
project confidence.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.440
Assure customers the problem will be solved
but be honest about the time it may take;

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:44.780
this includes situations in which you are
dealing with difficult customers.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.050
Thirdly, listen actively.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.829
Avoid interrupting a customer.

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:53.089
Fourth, be culturally sensitive.

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.750
Use titles when possible.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.219
Fifth, be on time.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:03.359
Sixth, avoid distractions such as personal
calls and social media messages while troubleshooting

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:04.670
a problem.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.540
Finally, keep confidential data confidential.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.290
Avoid the temptation to look at data that
is left out but should not be left out.

